  "attribution": "Cornell Lab of Ornithology, EOD - eBird Observation Dataset, 2024 annual edition via GBIF, DOI 10.15468/aomfnb. CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Isitusa derives county occurrence determinations; provider source bytes are retained without alteration.",
  "rationale": "MAIN independently reran both committed reviewer recipes and checked the complete 41-record source query, 41 original verbatim responses, taxonomy, explicit county/state identity, historical dates and source-method context. All five reviewed county pairs have qualified positive witnesses. Public original field support and program-level quality controls suffice without inventing a per-record human expert approval requirement. The opaque tag concordance is qualified metadata evidence, not an individual review decision.",
  "limitations": [
    "Historical 2024 recorded occurrence only; no current persistence, breeding, establishment, population size or invasive-impact claim.",
    "EOD omits sampling-effort and complete-checklist metadata. Source silence and unfinished acquisition never create absence or non-detection.",
    "The complete retained single-page query defines this bounded record scope, not all years, all eBird data, or a completed county protocol.",
    "Original county/state names resolve uniquely to current active county entries; coordinates are consistency evidence only. Missing coordinate uncertainty does not negate this explicit county authority.",
    "Matching dataset machine tags support a qualified annotation-propagation inference. The exact GBIF flattening transformation and individual human expert approval are not proved.",
    "Cornell asks for living unrestrained birds and permits suspected escapes. Home, park, hotel, golf-course or zoo locality words alone do not establish captivity; concrete record contradictions still require review.",
    "Multiple observers may report the same birds or event. Source record counts are not summed or described as independent sightings.",
    "The first verbatim response was successfully retained before a local parser-shape failure. It was reused, and the remaining 40 originals were acquired once; no failure bytes or code identities were rewritten.",
    "The context acquisition receipt pins its executed recipe but declares no repository commit. Earlier taxonomy metadata and later occurrence acquisition preserve their distinct actual commits."
